  "tagline": "GPU- and vector-accelerated database for real-time spatial, time-series and vector analytics.",
  "description": "Kinetica is a distributed, columnar, memory-first database that started as GPUdb for US Army intelligence workloads and vectorizes queries across GPUs or CPUs. Its niche is fast analytics on streaming, location-rich data: native geospatial and time-series functions, graph analytics, vector search and continuous materialized views, fed from Kafka at high rates. Newer releases add an LLM-driven SQL assistant and agent tooling. It is available as Kinetica Cloud, a free Developer Edition and an Enterprise edition. It is powerful for telemetry and geospatial use cases, but proprietary and niche outside them.",
